\par\par \b \uc2 Market Talk Roundup: \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Raises Rate by 25 Basis Points, Krona Drops\b0\par\par\uc2 1,156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2023\par 16:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Sweden's Riksbank\uc2  raised the policy rate by 25 basis points to 3.75% and signaled the need to increase rates further. Some had anticipated a bigger rise, however, and the Swedish krona reaches a record low against the euro later in the day. The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  announced a plan to hedge 25% of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which analysts consider will be insufficient to stop the krona's weakening. The following is a selection of analyst comments.\par \par \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Stresses Hedging Plan Isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 1350 GMT - In a surprise move, the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  said it is considering hedging part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to reduce financial risks, but governor Erik Thedeen repeatedly stated in Thursday's press conference that the measure was not to be seen as \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 SEB\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief strategist Olle Holmgren says in a note. "Considering that the measure was presented at the same time as the rate decision which states that a weaker SEK is the main upside risk for inflation...it seems probable that the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  hopes that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging will support the krona." EUR/SEK dropped back after the initial run higher this morning, but has headed higher again since Thedeen's comments, \uc2 SEB\uc2  says. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Swedish Krona Falls to Record Low Vs Euro as Rate Outlook Looks Uncertain\par \par \uc2 1327 GMT - The Swedish krona falls to a record low against the euro, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 , extending losses after the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  earlier hiked interest rates by 25 basis points to 3.75%, when some had anticipated a bigger 50bp increase. The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  faces similar challenges to other central banks but they are "more extreme," leaving substantial uncertainty about the future path of monetary policy, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  global economist \uc2 James Pomeroy\uc2  says in a note. "Inflation is still well-above its target, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains weak, and the economy is hardly growing in aggregate, with consumer spending falling sharply in recent quarters." \uc2 HSBC\uc2  expects data will justify a pause in rate rises in September. EUR/SEK hits a high of 11.8437, \uc2 FactSet\uc2  data show. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's Higher Rate Path Addresses Continued Inflation Risks\par \par \uc2 1125 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  stuck to its initial plan of raising its policy rate by 25 basis points but responded to the increased upside risk in inflation by raising the rate path by an additional 20 basis points, which was more than expected, \uc2 DNB Markets\uc2  economist Oddmund Berg says in a note. The new rate path peaks at 4.05%, implying another 25 basis points hike later this year and the probability of a final quarter-percentage point hike thereafter. "In our view, the increase [in rate path] is a direct result of international rates rising far more than expected in April and the upside risk to inflation if the SEK continues to weaken." (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Guidance Looks on the Hawkish Side\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's 25 basis points rate increase to 3.75% was widely expected, but its forward guidance is somewhat more hawkish than expected, \uc2 Swedbank\uc2  analysts say in a note. The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  now signals at least one more hike this year, and \uc2 Swedbank\uc2  expects 25 basis points in September and November, to a terminal rate of 4.25%. "We continue to view inflationary risks as tilted to the upside, not least due to the record weak SEK. That, coupled with surprisingly hawkish decisions from other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, is likely to keep the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  in hiking mode for longer." The resilient Swedish economy also makes it easier for the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to steer monetary policy toward further tightening, \uc2 Swedbank\uc2  says. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Hedging Plan Unlikely to Halt Krona's Fall\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's decision to hedge 25% of its SEK400 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will render a positive flow of up to SEK100 billion, which looks a modest amount and is unlikely to stop the trend of the Swedish krona falling, \uc2 SEB\uc2  chief strategist \uc2 Carl Hammer\uc2  says in a note. "However it is a sign that the weakened exchange rate is pressuring \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  and more measures could be implemented should we approach 12.00 in EUR/SEK." EUR/SEK last trades at 11.745, having briefly jupmed to a high of 11.8289 after the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  raised its policy rate by 25 basis points. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's 25Bps Rate Rise Disappointed, Weakening The Krona\par \par \uc2 0918 GMT - The Swedish krona weakened following the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's rate decision as some had hoped for a larger 50 basis points rate hike rather than the 25 basis points that was delivered, Handelsbanken senior economist Johan Lof says in a note. A practically unanimous economist consensus ahead of Thursday's decision saw the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  raising its key policy rate by 25 basis points, and that was the main scenario among market participants as well, he says. The quantitative tightening acceleration was also widely anticipated. "However, markets were pricing a non-trivial probability for an ultra-hawkish 50 basis points hike surprise, so despite the main scenario materialising, market interest rates declined and the krona weakened on impact."(dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Shows Hawkish Face With Rate Rise, Higher Path\par \par \uc2 0832 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  has shown its hawkish face by raising the policy rate 25 basis points to 3.75% and lifting the rate path by a further 30 basis points to peak at 4.05%, clearly outstripping its April forward guidance, Handelsbanken senior economist Johan Lof says in a note. Adding to the hawkish tilt today is the decision to accelerate the reduction of asset holdings. Despite the more restrictive policy, the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  revised its GDP forecast up, its unemployment forecast down and its CPIF excluding energy forecast up. "All told, that signals an increased awareness of a deeper entrenched inflation problem." Handelsbanken still sees two more 25 basis-point rate rises, in September and November, before cautious rate cuts begin next summer. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Swedish Krona Falls to Multi-Year Low Vs Euro After \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Raises Rates by 25Bps\par \par \uc2 0754 GMT - The Swedish krona falls to its weakest level in more than a decade after the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  raised its policy rate by 25 basis points to 3.75%, disappointing some in the market who had anticipated a bigger 50bp rise. The falls come even as the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  said rates would rise at least once more this year and opted to increase the pace of government-bond sales from September. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  separately announced it was considering hedging around a quarter of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. EUR/SEK rises to a peak of 11.8289 after the decision, its highest since 2009, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 , from around 11.7538 beforehand. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2023 10:02 ET (14:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230629ej6t002bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
