\par\par \b \uc2 Sweden's Riksbank\uc2  says 'jump', the crown says 'no'\b0\par\par\uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2023\par 08:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 3 (Reuters) -\par \par \uc2 Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried and failed to talk up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is running out of room to raise rates, leaving the crown languishing around its weakest in 14 years against the euro and undermining its efforts to control inflation.\par \par \uc2 It's not going to get much better any time soon. Markets are pricing for more rate hikes from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and others, which are hard for the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to match due to issues in the housing sector.\par \par \uc2 There is talk about possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the crown, though analysts think it unlikely the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  would resort to this tool in the near term, partly because of its limited reserves.\par \par \uc2 "We believe in, and want to have, a stronger crown," \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Governor Erik Thedeen told reporters last Wednesday after the bank announced a half-point rate hike to 3.50%.\par \par \uc2 "If that doesn't happen over time, it could have significance for monetary policy because a weaker crown could lead to higher inflation," he said.\par \par \uc2 Markets, however, were not listening. The crown weakened as much as 1% that day.\par \par \uc2 More broadly it has lost 14% in value against both the euro and the dollar since late 2021. In recent months, it has held up better against the dollar, but is trading around its weakest since 2008 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The problem, analysts say is markets expect more interest rate rises from the \uc2 ECB\uc2 , while the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  last week hinted it was nearly done with tightening and two rate-setters voted for a 25 basis point rate increase.\par \par \uc2 Kenneth Broux\uc2 , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  said this "dovish dissent" would mean "more weakness against the euro, as the rate differential moved in the euro's favour".\par \par \uc2 Traders currently expect 75 basis points more of tightening from the \uc2 ECB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Expectations for higher official interest rates typically boost money market and government bond yields, attracting investor cash to a country, which boosts the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The gap between key parts of the Swedish and euro zone rate curves narrowed sharply in 2022 and turned in the euro's favour at the start of this year.\par \par \uc2 TOUGH SPOT\par \par \uc2 The weakening crown is a problem for Sweden. It makes imported goods more expensive, thereby adding to inflation, which is already running at 8.9% year-on-year when volatile energy prices are excluded.\par \par \uc2 "The krona is not the major factor for elevated inflation, but it does play an important role and obviously it would be beneficial to have a strong exchange rate," said \uc2 Carl Hammer\uc2 , chief strategist at \uc2 SEB\uc2 , using the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Swedish name.\par \par \uc2 Hiking rates further would typically support a country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it's difficult in Sweden because rate rises have already brought long-standing problems with the housing sector to the fore.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  expects house prices to bottom out in early 2024 after falling around 19% from a peak in early 2022.\par \par \uc2 "It's difficult for the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to be that hawkish," said Jan von Gerich, chief analyst at \uc2 Nordea\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They have an inflation problem, but they also have a housing market that's already in a weak state, and an economy that is coming down."\par \par \uc2 Households in Sweden are more sensitive to rates than those elsewhere, as around 60% of mortgages are on floating rates.\par \par \uc2 That leaves the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  exploring other options to boost the crown.\par \par \uc2 "I think they will only hike, at the max, one more time. But I think they then increase (quantitative tightening) and then if that doesn't really help, definitely there will be some sort of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the table," said \uc2 SEB\uc2 's Hammer.\par \par \uc2 He said the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets seemed a way away.\par \par \uc2 Such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are rate. \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought crowns in 2001 to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and sold it in 2021 to replace the borrowed part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  analysts said the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's reserves make up less than two days\u8217\'20\'19 worth of daily market volume in dollar/crown and euro/crown trading, potentially limiting the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, SocGen's Broux said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "on his radar" as he'd been getting client questions about it.\par \par \uc2 He said the 11.50 crown-per euro level could be one to watch. It is currently at 11.29.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alun John and Harry Robertson; Editing by Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-3T07:15:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230503ej5300z18\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\pic