\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Sweden \highlight\uc2 's Riksbank\uc2  Decides Against Extending Mandate for Rapid  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2019\par 11:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1013 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  's Executive Board did not extend a mandate for rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that expired Tuesday. The decision indicates a further move away from a focus on the krona, and decreasing concern of rapid appreciation, according to Handelsbanken strategist Claes Mahlen. Worries about a fierce appreciation of the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have receded in view of the krona's rapid decline in the past few weeks. The krona, however, strengthened earlier Wednesday as the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  confirmed its intention to lift the key rate in the second half of the year. ( nina.adam@wsj.com, @Nina_Adam_)\par \par \uc2 0953 GMT - Lower-than-expected inflation data in the U.K. isn't enough to push the pound lower as investors remain focused on uncertainty surrounding Brexit. January's year-on-year consumer price index fell below \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  's 2.0% target for the first time in two years to 1.8% from 2.1% in December. A WSJ poll had forecast a smaller fall to 1.9%. Core CPI remained steady and as expected at 1.9%. The pound is around the same level is was before the release, last down 0.1% at $1.2889. EUR/GBP is up 0.1% at 0.8787. On Monday, the U.K. gross domestic product also came in weaker than expected, which sent the pound lower. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT - Inflation data is likely to have dropped in the U.S. due to cheaper oil prices, which should keep EUR/USD "range-locked," says Kit Juckes, macro strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . The euro dipped below $1.13 at the beginning of the week as the dollar strengthened slightly, but is now back in the range it had been earlier--between 1.13 and 1.15--and is last flat at $1.1323. The January headline U.S. consumer price index is expected to fall to 1.5% year-on-year from 1.9% a month ago, according to a WSJ poll. Core CPI is expected to fall to 2.1% from 2.2%. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT - German two-year bonds, or Schatz, look a logical alternative, at least in the short term, to expensive 10-year Bunds, which it's time to cash in on, \uc2 DZ Bank\uc2  analyst Daniel Lenz says. Ten-year Bund yields currently trade at a yield of 0.125%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  , having recently touched 0.08%, the lowest level since 2016. The two-year Schatz yield trades at -0.57%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . The 10-year Bund yield fall is mainly attributable to the deteriorating economic environment in Germany and the eurozone, Mr. Lenz says, adding that Schatz yields haven't replicated this movement. "Quite the opposite," he says, adding that Schatz yields have risen about four bps over the same period. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  won't extend the mandate to quickly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to counteract rapid krona strengthening, as the krona has weakened since December and was 3% off the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  's forecast ahead of Wednesday's meeting, says Claes Mahlen at Handelsbanken. "This indicates a further move away from the focus on the krona and less worries of fast appreciation." The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  left policy rates and the rate path unchanged, but revised growth forecasts slightly lower. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still sees the next 25 basis point rate increase in October, but the market prices this in April 2020. Handelsbanken expects the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to carry out the signaled hike in October, with the repo rate staying at zero throughout 2020. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0904 GMT - The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  has acknowledged subdued economic growth in Sweden, but reiterated it is going to increase interest rates in the second half of 2019, pushing the Swedish krona higher. EUR/SEK falls to one-week low of 10.4394 from 10.4909 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to keep repo rate unchanged at minus 0.25%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that "economic activity is still strong" in Sweden and that the "conditions for inflation to remain close to 2% in the coming years have not changed to any great extent." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0859 GMT - Italy's 10-year government bond, or BTP, appears to be eliciting buyers at yields around 3%, says \uc2 Natixis\uc2  rates strategist Jean-Christophe Machado. However, when the yield spread over Bunds falls to 250 basis points, "caution is in order," Mr. Machado says. Italy's 10-year benchmark BTP trades at a yield of 2.852%, while the 10-year BTP-Bund spread is 272 basis points, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0850 GMT - The greenback has edged through support in Asia trading in the S$1.3560 area, and whether that holds could depend on Friday's Singapore GDP revision. If data show the city-state's economy is holding steady, it may drag the pair closer to its next support level of S$1.3450. Resistance remains near its 50-day moving average of around S$1.3600. The greenback is down 0.1% today. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0836 GMT - The cost of three-month sterling options--which help investors protect themselves against large moves in the pound--has risen slightly, but it is still much lower than it was during mid-December last year. This suggests investors are now less worried about a disorderly Brexit. The cost of one-month sterling options has gone down. Still, companies and fund managers are more worried now than they were same time a year ago, given that the cost of three-month options has increased since January 2018. The U.K. parliament is due to vote on the Brexit withdrawal deal again on Thursday. The current Brexit deadline is March 29. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT - \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  expects U.K.'s consumer price index inflation--data which will be released at 0930 GMT--to fall from 2.1% to the inflation target at 2%, exactly two years since the target was last reached. It expects core CPI to stay at 1.9% and the commodity part of the CPI basket to fall. "Food-price inflation seems to have bottomed out and might eke out a very modest increase but the dominant effect will be a fall of 1.5% month-on-month in fuel prices," SocGen says. This should shave off nearly 0.1 percentage point from CPI inflation, SocGen says, although it warns there's some risk that the figure will remain at 2.1% year on year. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0822 GMT - Spanish bond yields are trading at their lowest in a year at around 1.24%, despite the elevated uncertainty around the upcoming budget vote and the possibility of snap elections, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  says. Spain's Socialist Party-controlled governing coalition needs votes from smaller parties to get majority to pass its spending plans, but some smaller, Catalan parties are likely to vote against the measure, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  says. Government sources have already indicated that the ruling Socialist Party will call snap elections if the budget vote fails, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  adds. The 10-year Spanish bond yield last trades at 1.25%, while the 10-year Spanish-German spread is 112 basis points, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com;)\par \par \uc2 0805 GMT - The supply outlook for the \uc2 European Financial Stability Facility\uc2  is benign for the coming weeks with no new supply until April, say \uc2 Citi\uc2 's strategists. The EFSF's EUR4.5 billion issuance in a dual-tranche transaction on Tuesday brought its year-to-date bond issuance to EUR7.5 billion, meaning that it has completed funding for the first quarter. "With this, the quarter with the highest amount of gross supply in 2019 has already been concluded successfully," \uc2 Citi\uc2  says. There is no EFSF supply until April when historically low 2Q funding needs start being raised, \uc2 Citi\uc2 's strategists say. The EFSF has penciled in EUR4 billion long-term issuance for 2Q. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 13, 2019 05:13 ET (10:13 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020190213ef2d001cc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
