\par\par \b \uc2 IMF\uc2  says \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  should not use  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  to ease policy\b0\par\par\uc2 97 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2016\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM, Sept 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has room to cut interest rates and expand its QE programe if it needs to make policy easier, but should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the crown is moderately undervalued, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be "a last resort," the leader of the \uc2 IMF\uc2  delegation, Craig Beaumont, said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  published its annual report on Sweden.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Simon Johnson; Editing by Daniel Dickson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-9-29T10:24:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160929ec9t00hd5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
