\par\par \b \uc2 NORDIC MORNING BRIEFING: Eyes on \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  Minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jens Hansegard \par \uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2016\par 07:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par 0830 Riksbank Minutes \par 0830 Sweden Ind Prod \par 0900 Norway Ind Prod \par  \par Nordic Equities \par 0700 Norwegian Air Traffic \par  \par In Focus: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Friday, Nordic investors will scrutinize the minutes from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  December rate setting meeting. November industrial production data from Norway and Sweden may also draw attention.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The corporate agenda is thin, but airline investors will look at \uc2 Norwegian Air Shuttle\uc2 's December traffic data.\par \par \uc2 Outside the region, investors will keep a close watch on China's ongoing market turmoil and on non-farm payrolls data from the U.S. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par 0550 GMT 9.6720-70 \par Previous 9.7093-143 \par %Chg -0.38 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par 0550 GMT 9.2285-385 \par Previous 9.2484-584 \par %Chg -0.22 \par  \par USD/NOK \par 0550 GMT 8.8883-943 \par Previous 8.8806-66 \par %Chg +0.09 \par  \par USD/SEK \par 0550 GMT 8.4811-901 \par Previous 8.4596-686 \par %Chg +0.25 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will examine the minutes from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's December rate setting meeting, at which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left its repo rate unchanged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, events since that meeting have somewhat overshadowed the importance of the minutes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On January 4, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Sweden\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  prepared for direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying it had clarified how the bank would make such decisions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fall in oil prices is hitting the Norwegian krone, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. Brent crude has reached lows not seen in over 11 years,\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In contrast, the Swedish krona is gaining on the back of safe-haven demand, the bank said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par  OMXN40 1,477.58 -2.1% \par  OMXS30 1,357.12 -2.2% \par  OBX    498.56   -2.9% \par  OMXC20 985.40   -1.8% \par  OMXH25 3,179.13 -2.3% \par  \par  \par Brent crude rose $0.43 to $34.18 \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic Markets closed lower Thursday, amid a wide sell-off and worries about the Chinese economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Denmark's Pandora bucked the trend and gained 4.5% after pre-announced full-year 2015 sales figures. The figures imply a very strong fourth quarter, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Cazenove\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the oil price slumping to multi-year lows, Norway's oil-heavy OBX index and the country's oil service companies posted the biggest losses in the region. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures prices made a mild turnaround in early Asia trade but the market remains on edge as fears of more volatility in the Chinese economy are keeping traders cautious.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices plunged to a more than a decade low on Thursday after the Chinese government allowed the yuan to fall faster than anticipated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 , light, sweet crude futures for delivery in February traded at $33.76 a barrel at 0240 GMT, up $0.49 in the Globex electronic session. February Brent crude on London's \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures exchange rose $0.43 to $34.18 a barrel. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Denmark's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its main interest rate on Thursday, as it sought to stay calibrated with recent policy moves by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in order to keep the Danish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steady against the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , known as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danmarks Nationalbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , raised its deposit rate to minus 0.65% from minus 0.75% as it began a slow retreat from a period of record-low borrowing costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Danish pharmaceutical company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Novo Nordisk\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NOVO-B.KO) said it has filed for regulatory approval in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  of a treatment for the blood clotting disorder haemophilia B.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Danish jeweler Pandora A/S plans to add 200 to 300 stores each year between 2016 and 2018 and will increase its focus on earrings following a similar move to promote rings which the company says has now seen the products become an established product line along with its charms and bracelets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Danish brewer Carlsberg A/S (CARL-A.KO) said it has appointed Heine Dalsgaard as its new chief financial officer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Charles Duxbury at charles.duxbury@wsj.com; Twitter: @WSJNordics\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 08, 2016 01:30 ET (06:30 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160108ec18000kn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw17