\par\par \b \uc2 Swedish cbank\uc2  nearing  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  - minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2016\par 09:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM, Jan 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  debated the next step for loosening monetary policy further, with several board members highlighting the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , minutes of the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's latest meeting showed on Friday.               \par \par \uc2 On Dec. 15, the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  held its benchmark repo rate unchanged at a record low of -0.35 percent and said it was ready to ease policy further if weak inflation in November proves to be longer lasting.               \par \par \uc2 Deputy Governor Per Jansson already then said there were arguments supporting further easing, for example in the form of another repo rate cut.               \par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  remains highly prepared to make monetary policy even more expansionary, even between the ordinary monetary policy meetings," a statement on the minutes said.               \par \par \uc2 "Several members also noted that if the exchange rate appreciated too rapidly, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be necessary," it said.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-8T09:54:26.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160108ec1800anz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
