\par\par \b \uc2 BREAKINGVIEWS- \highlight22\uc2 Sweden \highlight\uc2  ignores Swiss lesson on  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 16:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (The author is a Reuters Breakingviews columnist. The opinions expressed are her own.)\par \par \uc2 By Swaha Pattanaik\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 5 (Reuters Breakingviews) - History's lessons are often ignored. Sweden may be the latest to do so by threatening to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the inflation-dampening strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the crown.\par \par \uc2 The clearest sign that the Nordic nation is ready and willing to act came on Jan. 4 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , known as the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 , gave its governor, Stefan Ingves, the power to sell crowns for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a nascent rise in inflation needed protection. It's easy to see why Ingves, who dismissed the option of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November 2014, may have had a change of heart.\par \par \uc2 The trade-weighted measure of the crown's value has appreciated about 6.5 percent since August 2015, making imported goods ever cheaper. Hardly helpful for a country where consumer prices have basically flatlined for the past three years.\par \par \uc2 Monetary policy could always be eased further, but cutting rates from their current record low of minus 0.35 percent carries risks for an economy which the government expects will grow by 3.1 percent this year. In particular, it risks boosting household debt, which has already surpassed 175 percent of disposable income. Focusing on weakening the exchange rate would avoid this danger.\par \par \uc2 The impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be short-lived. A 2006 study published in the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's working paper series found Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 1993 and 2002 did little to reverse, accentuate, or moderate exchange rate moves.\par \par \uc2 Then there is the more recent example of Switzerland, which spectacularly abandoned attempts to cap its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost exactly a year ago after a protracted and dogged fight. Few traders expect the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to put up as much of a fight as its Swiss peer, whose balance sheet ballooned to around 80 percent of the country's GDP before it capitulated.\par \par \uc2 None of this may prevent the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Like other central banks, low inflation is forcing it to pull all the levers at its disposal, no matter how useless they are.\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Jan. 4 gave its chief the formal power to act immediately to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to help push up inflation.\par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was still prepared to take other measures "in addition to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if this is necessary for inflation to stabilise around 2 per cent".\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/1Rp96kS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/1Rp96kS}}}\par \par \uc2 - 2006 working paper on \uc2 Riksbank\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/1myPVKu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/1myPVKu}}}\par \par \uc2 Reuters: \uc2 Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes step closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 RELATED COLUMNS\par \par \uc2 Shades of tragedy\par \par \uc2 Brownian motion\par \par \uc2 Foundering faith\par \par \uc2 - For previous columns by the author, Reuters customers can click on\par \par \uc2 (Editing by John Foley and \uc2 Sarah Bailey\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-8T15:46:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160105ec1500izg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
