\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Swedish cbank\uc2  ready for  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  after crown strengthening - Ingves\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2015\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM, Dec 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to start \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the recent strengthening of the crown if needed, Governor Stefan Ingves said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The appreciation of the crown jeopardized the upturn in inflation and the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  had "a high level of preparedness to act", he said in an unscheduled statement.\par \par \uc2 The crown has strengthened since the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  on Dec. 15 held its benchmark repo rate unchanged at a record low of -0.35 percent and said its bond purchasing programme that was last expanded in October would run as planned.\par \par \uc2 The daily calculated crown index had strengthened to 108.22 on Wednesday, levels the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  forecasted to be reached around the first quarter in 2017.\par \par \uc2 The crown weakened around 3 ore versus the euro after the announcement, to 9.16 at 1135 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  has repeatedly warned that a quick strengthening of the crown could warrant action - including \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the strong crown was the main reason behind an out-of-schedule rate cut and expansion of the bond purchases in March.\par \par \uc2 "The recent appreciation in the Swedish krona creates risks for the upturn in inflation. If the exchange rate strengthens earlier and more rapidly than forecast, it will be more difficult to push up inflation towards the target," Ingves said.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  is therefore highly prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the exchange market whenever we deem it necessary", he added.\par \par \uc2 The last time the \uc2 Riksbank\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was in 2001. At that time, the problem was the opposite: a weakening Swedish crown meant there was a risk of higher inflation ahead than the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's 2 percent target.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  is clearly not satisfied with the crown and if strengthening continues, they might act at any time. You have to take their word for it," said Swedbank analyst Knut Hallberg.\par \par \uc2 "They might act during the next coming days, an action that could have a big market impact due to the thin holiday trade," he said.\par \par \uc2 A few days before the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2 's latest rate decision, data suggested the uptick in Swedish inflation appeared to have stalled in November when underlying consumer prices fell 0.1 percent from the previous month. (Reporting by Daniel Dickson, Johan Sennero and Sven Nordenstam; Editing by Alistair Scrutton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-2T11:53:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151230ebcu00ci1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
