\par\par \b \uc2 Swedish cbank\uc2  governor Ingves says ready for  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  after SEK strengthening\b0\par\par\uc2 122 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2015\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM, Dec 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stefan Ingves said on Wednesday the recent appreciation of the crown jeopardised the upturn in inflation and that the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  had a high level of preparedness to act.\par \par \uc2 "The recent appreciation in the Swedish krona creates risks for the upturn in inflation. If the exchange rate strengthens earlier and more rapidly than forecast, it will be more difficult to push up inflation towards the target," Ingves said in an unscheduled statement.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  is therefore highly prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the exchange market whenever we deem it necessary", he added.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Daniel Dickson)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-2T10:37:47.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151230ebcu00b9l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
