\par\par \b \uc2 *Sweden Riksbank Cuts Repo Rate To -0.25% and Buys Government Bonds For SEK30B\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 13:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:49 ET *Sweden Riksbank Repo Rate Cut, Govt Bond Buys to Support Upturn in Inflation\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:49 ET *Sweden Riksbank: Signs Inflation Has Bottomed and is Rising, But Recent SEK Appreciation Risks Breaking Trend\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:53 ET *Sweden Riksbank to Buy Bonds Worth SEK30B With Maturities up to 25 Yrs, To Run 26 March-May 2015\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:54 ET *Sweden Riksbank: Repo Rate Expected to Remain at -0.25% At Least Until 2H16\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:55 ET *Sweden Riksbank: After 2H16, Rate Expected to Rise Gradually and Slower Than Forecast in Feb\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:55 ET *Sweden Riksbank: Ready To Make Monetary Policy Even More Expansionary If Necessary\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:56 ET *Sweden Riksbank: Repo Rate Could Possibly Be Cut Further, Could Buy Even More Govt Bonds\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:57 ET *Sweden Riksbank Is Also Prepared To Launch Programme Of Loans To Companies Via Banks\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 08:58 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  Riksbank: Other Possible Measures Include \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or Buying Other Types of Assets\par \par \uc2 18 Mar 2015 09:11 ET  Sweden Cuts Main Interest Rate to -0.25%, Increases Bond-Buying Program\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jens Hansegard \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 STOCKHOLM--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday cut its main interest rate further into negative territory and said it's increasing its bond-buying program to counter recent krona appreciation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Riksbank, the world's oldest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , lowered its benchmark rate to minus 0.25% from minus 0.1% and said it would buy government bonds worth 30 billion Swedish kronor ($3.41 billion). The repurchase rate had stood at minus 0.1% since February.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There are signs that inflation has bottomed out and is beginning to rise, but the recent appreciation of the krona risks breaking this trend," the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a statement. The Riksbank targets 2% inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In response to the move, the Swedish krona weakened against the euro, which rose to 9.32 kronor from 9.17 kronor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jens Hansegard at jens.hansegard@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 18, 2015 09:11 ET (13:11 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150318eb3i001qs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
