\par\par \b \uc2 Swedish c.bank's Jansson: SEK has strengthened sharply, can't rule out  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 14:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's crown has appreciated sharply since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut rates and announced a bond-buying programme in mid-February, Deputy Riksbank Governor Per Jansson said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "I think we have had now a sharp appreciation," he said.\par \par \uc2 Jansson told reporters recently a sharp appreciation of the crown would be "game over" in terms of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  being able to meet its 2 percent inflation target.\par \par \uc2 Jansson did not rule out the Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "It's part of the package. We cannot rule out anything so it's certainly part of the package we've discussed along with other measures, but it's hard to discuss single elements of the package but it's certainly there as a point that's being discussed," he said.\par \par \uc2 At it last meeting in February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key repo rate into negative territory, launched bond purchases and said it could take further steps to battle falling prices. (Reporting by Yasmeen Abutaleb; writing by Simon Johnson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-6T14:40:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150306eb3600elj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
