\par\par \b \uc2 Further Riksbank Policy Measures Likely, Says DNB -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2015\par 12:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1117 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The \uc2 Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to take further policy steps to lift inflation closer to its 2% target, Norwegian bank DNB says in a note Thursday. The main \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is now at zero, so long-term fixed rate loans to banks will likely be the Riksbank's preferred option as this has been done before, in 2009, DNB says. This could be combined with a negative repo rate, DNB adds. There is also a "significant probability" that the Riksbank might buy assets, DNB says, despite the limited range of assets available in \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unlikely, DNB says. (charles.duxbury@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 1109 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Switzerland's largest regional, state-guaranteed bank \uc2 Zuercher Kantonalbank\uc2  will start charging large institutional clients to hold Swiss francs. The ZKB will impose a fee of 0.75% on deposits after the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's decision last week to let the franc to float free versus the euro, although this won't affect private savers or small businesses, as long as the SNB doesn't sharpen policy, it says. This follows a similar move this week by Geneva-based \uc2 Lombard Odier\uc2 , one of the country's oldest banks. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1108 GMT The Hungarian forint is awaiting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's announcement scheduled for 1330 GMT at a strengthened position versus the euro. EUR/HUF is trading at this year's lowest level, at 314.40. Government bond yields also declined across the curve, the short-end segment of the curve was especially strong, CIB Says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects a favorable bond buying program to give HUF further strength, eying the level 310 last seen in late December. (veronika.gulyas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1107 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Investors are in a gloomy mood, says Benoit Anne at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 , after a trip to Central Eastern Europe. "The scars left by the major SNB move are still fresh. Meanwhile, there is a great deal of anticipation but also quite a bit of nervousness surrounding the ECB's potential announcement," he says. On top of it, the Greek election this week should create some disruptive noise. Still, he expects the ECB to trigger a rally in emerging market assets. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6:02 EST - Itau says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has left the door open for more rate hikes as policy makers are concerned about inflation pressures from regulated prices such as electric energy and fuel. But it notes as economic activity remains weak and "significant fiscal consolidation is on track...there are incipient signs of deceleration in service inflation." As such it sees a quarter-point rate hike at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's next meeting after half-point ones the prior 2. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1058 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Today's ECB decision will have an impact well beyond the euro exchange rate, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  reminds. "The ECB will set the tone for EUR/PLN, if President Draghi confirms a full-scale QE," the bank says. Its baseline scenario assumes Draghi may only pre-announce QE today. "For the market which is already far more cautious following the December squeeze, this may not prove sufficient for EUR/PLN to end the day below the 4.26/24 support zone, especially if we are left with plenty of unanswered questions," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. Adds if markets end up disappointed with the ECB, the December high at EUR/PLN 4.40 could be back in focus. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1054 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opens the door for more rate hikes as it takes out the word "parsimoniously" from its rate decision statement, says Neil Shearing, an economist at Capital Economics, who increases his Selic rate peak view to 12.75% from 12.25%. "Policymakers have used such language [parsimoniously] in the past to signal that the end of the tightening cycle is approaching. Its removal suggests that further rate hikes are now likely," he says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised Selic rate Wednesday to 12.25% from 11.75%, reaching the highest level in more than three years. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1051 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  outlines the main scenarios and outcomes ahead of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate setting and monetary policy announcement. The first is of substantial disappointment, if the ECB delays quantitative easing. In this case the euro will rally since the ECB would merely be delaying inevitable future easing, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists say. If the ECB's announcement is in-line with consensus, "little initial reaction as this was likely already in the price," they say. However, the euro will weaken over time. Finally, a scenario in which the surprise will be greater than expected: unsurprisingly, this would push the euro significantly lower. The move would just be the prelude of a long-term downtrend. The speed of decline, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  reminds, will be data dependent.(chiara.albanese@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1039 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The March gilt contract trades 1 point lower at 121.35, pushing the yield on the 10-year cash 10 bps higher to 1.58%, after the ONS released data showing U.K. borrowing rose. Data showed UK PSNB rose to GBP13.1 billion against consensus of GBP9.7 billion and GBP10.3 billion a year ago. Core fixed income is also under pressure ahead of the ECB meeting and expected QE announcement in case of any disappointment which would knock bonds from their current lofty valuations. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1034 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's military-appointed government is ready to spend over 25 billion baht ($766.8 million) to help boost natural rubber price to 80 baht ($2.45) per kilo, according to Deputy Prime Minister General Prawit Wongsuwan. Prawit met with the country's major rubber business operators. "The private sector has resolved to agree with the increase of the rubber price, which will be gradual, until it reaches 80 baht," says Prawit. Currently, Thailand's central rubber market auction price of ribbed smoked sheet is at around $1.9 per kilo. Col. Winthai Suvaree, an army spokesman, says that the budget, which has earlier approved by the cabinet, will mostly come from state-run banks while less than 10% of the money will be contributed by the budget of the National Rubber Policy Committee.(nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1033 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Quantitative easing in itself can't solve problems, said Michala Marcussen, global head of economics at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  Corporate & Investment Banking to journalists in Frankfurt Thursday, adding that it could be even be counter-productive in an aging society. "The low yields lead to higher savings, and they do that at the expense of consumption," she says. Ms. Marcussen adds the eurozone needs to carry out structural and fiscal reforms to generate sustainable economic growth. (herbert.rude@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1031 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Nigeria's naira hits an all-time low of over 191 against the U.S. dollar, weighed by the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closing off various channels for changing money in yet another attempt to combat the effects of tumbling oil prices. The naira has now fallen 15% over the last six months and around 4.2% since the start of 2015 alone. (josie.cox@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 22, 2015 06:17 ET (11:17 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150122eb1m0023e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
