\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Sweden Fin Min: Ways To Recapitalize EU Banks Vital\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2011\par 13:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 07:59 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Sees More Opennesss To Act On Banks At EU Level\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 07:59 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Fixes To Banks' Problems Must Come Within Month\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 07:59 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Sweden's Low Level Of Debt Gives Security\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 08:00 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Ways Of Restructuring EU Banks Vital\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 08:00 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Krona A Bit More Stable Than Previously\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 08:00 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Worsening Of European Debt Crisis Would Hit SEK\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 08:00 EDT *DJ  Sweden Fin Min: Weaker SEK During Last Crisis Helped Sweden\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 08:01 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fin Min: Strong SEK Was Worry After SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 5 Oct 2011 08:33 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Sees More Openness On Bank Fixes At EU Level\par \par \uc2 STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--Swedish Finance Minister Anders Borg Wednesday said it is vital that agreements are reached on ways to handle struggling banks in Europe, adding that he sees more openness at European Union level to find solutions following the recent meeting of EU finance ministers.\par \par \uc2 "We have to get these backstops in place--structures for recapitalizing and restructuring banks," Borg told reporters in Stockholm. "What was positive with yesterday's meeting was that there was a greater openness to acting on an EU-level on these questions than previously."\par \par \uc2 He added that "a solution must be found within a month."\par \par \uc2 Moving to Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Borg said a worsening of the European debt crisis would weaken the krona, but it has been "a bit more stable than previously" during the market turbulence.\par \par \uc2 The weakening of the krona during the financial crisis which began in 2008 helped stabilize Sweden's economy, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Especially within the forestry industry -- it helped with jobs," he said.\par \par \uc2 Borg said the strength of the krona after the recent move by the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  to limit the Swiss franc's strength against the euro had been a concern, but it only lasted a few days.\par \par \uc2 Pegging the krona to the euro would be the "worst of all worlds," Borg said.\par \par \uc2 "The advantage of being in the euro zone is that you have access to the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financing and you get security for your banking system. If you just peg the krona you lose the airbag effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and you don't get the stability of being part of the ECB's system," he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Charles Duxbury, Dow Jones Newswires; +46-8-5451-3092; charles.duxbury@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 05, 2011 08:33 ET (12:33 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111005e7a5003i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
