\par\par \b \uc2  Riksbank says June  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  helped crown, CPI. \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2001\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, Nov 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, said on Friday its crown purchases in June had helped break the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steep fall and contributed to lowering inflation expectations. \par \par \uc2  In minutes of board meetings held on June 14 and July 5, released on Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which it bought a total of 12 billion Swedish crowns ($1.13 billion), were necessary to send a signal to the market that it was taking its inflation target seriously. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank had been concerned that because of its strong impact on import prices, the weakening crown would boost inflation above its goal of two percent over a 12-24 month rolling horizon. \par \par \uc2  The underlying inflation index, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely monitors in its interest rate decisions jumped to a seven-year high of 3.1 percent in May. \par \par \uc2  The bank said it sold 300 million euros and $190 million on June 15, a further 170 million euros and $240 million on June 18 and another 100 million euros and $200 million on June 25. \par \par \uc2  "Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  there were no clear signs of rising inflation, higher inflation expectations or increased long-term interest rate differentials in relation to other countries," the Riksbank said in the minutes. \par \par \uc2  "Nor has the depreciation of the crown accelerated, rather the reverse. This indicates that the credibility of the inflation target has certainly not been affected negatively." \par \par \uc2  To reinforce the effects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the key repo rate by 25 basis points to 4.25 percent in July at a time when many other central banks were cutting theirs to help slowing economies. \par \par \uc2  "The dramatic depreciation of the crown ceased after the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and the repo rate hike in July. The crown appreciated slightly until mid-August, when new data and developments on the financial markets indicated that the economic slowdown in Sweden and abroad would be more pronounced," the Riksbank said. \par \par \uc2  "Inflation expectations, when measured according to Statistics Sweden's survey of household purchasing plans, also fell slightly. The indications of weaker economic activity probably contributed to the latter." \par \par \uc2  Since June 2000 the crown has weakened by 24 percent against the dollar and 15 percent against the euro as foreign investors pulled out of the technology-laden Stockholm bourse and Swedish pension funds invested more abroad, taking advantage of new regulations. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011130dxbu01xr8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
