\par\par \b \uc2  Swedish PM sees fundamentals underpinning crown. \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2001\par 18:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NORRKOPING, Sweden, Aug 23 (Reuters) - Prime Minister Goran Persson said on Thursday his Social Democratic government's firm fiscal policy and Sweden's healthy economic fundamentals should positively underpin the recently ailing crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are conducting a firm fiscal policy, our inflation is low and we are competitive. That ought to give those who are watching the crown a positive picture of the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Persson told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  The Swedish unit hit all-time lows close to 9.50 crowns per euro earlier this week, marking a slide of six percent in the past three months, eight percent year-to-date and 18 percent from its record highs set in May last year. \par \par \uc2  At 1630 GMT on Thursday, it was trading around 9.44 per euro. \par \par \uc2  "It is politically opportunistic to believe, as the right-wing (opposition) parties do, that you can launch some kind of programme to shore up the crown exchange rate," Persson said, underlining that the crown was floating freely and that it was up to market forces to determine its external value. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in June, justifying its support purchases of crowns for euros and dollars by saying the domestic unit's depreciation could threaten its two-percent inflation target. \par \par \uc2  Persson reiterated that he could not exclude Swedish membership of the euro by 2005 and said the entry requirement of two years of exchange rate stability would not be a problem. \par \par \uc2  "It is a factor that must be assessed. But it is a long time until then, we will make it," he said. \par \par \uc2  Persson said it was premature to begin discussing at what exchange rate the Swedish crown should be pegged to the euro although he noted that the issue would be important for the Swedish export industry. \par \par \uc2  The Social Democrats have promised to let the people decide the issue of euro membership in a referendum on an unspecified date. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010823dx8n00ywe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
