\par\par \b \uc2  Goldman Sachs sees Swedish crown strengthening. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2001\par 15:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, July 19 (Reuters) - Investment bank Goldman Sachs said on Thursday the Swedish crown seemed to have broken out of its recent weakening spiral and was going to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the weakness in the Swedish economy it looks as though the fundamental capital flows have turned in the crown's favour," Goldman Sachs said in a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysis. \par \par \uc2  Goldman Sachs sees the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firming to 8.80 against the euro on a 12-month horizon compared with 9.2450 at 1250 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "We would expect the crown to appreciate on a trade-weighted basis in coming months," it said. "Overall, crown weakness seems to have passed. \par \par \uc2  At 1250 GMT, Sweden's inverted trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket index was 0.2 percent up on the day near three-week highs. \par \par \uc2  It was 1.6 percent up on all-time lows set in mid-June but 5.9 percent down so far in 2001 and 15 percent off year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  Repeated support \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last month and its 25 basis point key rate rise to 4.25 percent early in July did not turn the crown onto a stronger path, but Goldman Sachs said the measures had not been in vain. \par \par \uc2  "In recent weeks the tightening of monetary policy combined with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Riksbank and a much healthier broad balance of payments position have helped to slow the crown's depreciating trend," it said. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting pension reform, which allowed pension funds to allocate more to foreign equities, Swedes have bought 96.5 billion crowns worth of foreign stocks in first five months of 2001, up from 4.9 billion crowns over the same period a year. \par \par \uc2  "Back in November we estimated that total pension reform outflow could be 84 billion crowns and if this is accurate it looks like most of the reform has already been done," Goldman Sachs said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010719dx7j00pv7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
