\par\par \b \uc2  No respite seen for Swedish crown despite rate hike. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 813 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2001\par 16:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 6 (Reuters) - The crown fell to record lows against the dollar after Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked interest rates on Friday and was expected to remain in the dog house with the Riksbank fighting a losing battle to prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Several bouts of crown-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Riksbank, \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have failed to give the Swedish crown any lasting support, prompting the bank to raise its key rate a quarter point to 4.25 percent earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has expressed its concern that the crown's weakness is fuelling inflation, which is already at a seven-year high and well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's two percent one-two year target range. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the Riksbank was fighting a losing battle. They added that the quarter-point rate hike was not enough to reverse capital outflows that have hurt the Swedish crown and the Riksbank was unable to tighten monetary policy further when growth was slowing. \par \par \uc2  "The Riksbank is in a no-win situation where it would have been damned if it hiked rates and damned if it didn't," said David Brown, chief economist at Bear Stearns International in London. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't worked means the Riksbank has resorted to monetary tightening to control inflation but it is fighting a losing battle." \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank said last month that it would hike rates if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges did not succeed in halting crown weakness. \par \par \uc2  Brown said the Swedish crown was set for further weakness and expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to test 9.40 against the euro over the next three months. The crown hit 2-1/2 year lows against the euro around 9.34 last month, before the first of the Riksbank's three bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its support. \par \par \uc2  Brown's forecast compares with three-day lows set around 9.27 per euro set earlier and came on a day when the euro had itself set eight-month troughs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  RIKSBANK IN A CORNER \par \par \uc2  Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken a hit from heavy capital outflows in recent months, following changes allowing Swedish pension funds to invest more overseas and recent weakness in Sweden's tech-laden stock market. \par \par \uc2  Against this backdrop, it was difficult for the Riksbank to take action to support the Swedish crown, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's OMX stock index fell to its lowest in more than a week on Friday, hurt by recent profit warnings from European technology firms. \par \par \uc2  In Sweden, technology-related stocks account for just under half of the main stock market index, one of the highest concentrations in the world. \par \par \uc2  "There is a strong correlation between Sweden's stock exchange and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Inward investment into Sweden has deteriorated sharply," said Hans Redeker, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in London. \par \par \uc2  Redeker said the crown was likely to weaken towards 9.45 against the euro in the next couple of months. \par \par \uc2  GROWTH WORRIES \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Riksbank's rate increase could also weigh on the Swedish crown by exacerbating concerns about growth. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank is one of the only central banks that has not cut rates this year in the face of a global slowdown. The Federal Reserve has cut rates six times and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which like the Riksbank faces high inflation, has trimmed rates once. \par \par \uc2  "It is clear that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't worked and that the Riksbank needed to hike rates to keep its credibility with markets," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  "But Sweden's economy is slowing and a rate rise is perceived as a bad thing by investors." \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank expects the Swedish economy to grow 2.2 percent in 2001 and 2.5 percent in 2002. \par \par \uc2  Traders added that further rate increases, by raising costs for firms, would put more pressure on Swedish stocks and thereby the crown. \par \par \uc2  "Markets think 25 basis points is not enough to stabilise the crown so will price in higher rates, which is bad for equity markets," said Redeker from BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Riksbank might provide some brief support for the crown, while any signs that the Riksbank was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again could weigh heavily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If the Riksbank doesn't come in again, the market could see the Swedish crown as a one-way bet," said Bank One's Shea. \par \par \uc2  The crown has been in a downtrend against the euro since May 2000, when it hit highs around 8.0430 - over 10 percent stronger than current levels. It has also been on a downtrend against the dollar since 1996 when it hit highs around 6.4250 crown per dollar - more than 40 percent stronger than current levels. \par