\par\par \b \uc2  Swedish crown woes may worsen if Riksbank hikes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 747 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2001\par 15:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 3 (Reuters) - The Swedish crown could suffer if the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, raises interest rates this week in a bid to rescue a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has failed to draw much lasting benefit from repeated rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the Riksbank is expected to leave rates unchanged at Thursday's policy meeting, with an announcement due on Friday, it said last month that it would hike rates if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets did not suceed in halting crown weakness. \par \par \uc2  Its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy crowns for dollars and euros on June 15, 18 and 25 has not been able to break an entrenched downtrend in the crown which has headed back toward record lows against the dollar and 2-1/2 year lows against the euro. \par \par \uc2  While some wonder whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could tighten policy as soon as this week, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said the move would only undermine the crown by exacerbating an economic slowdown already underway in \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Option one of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed and option two of raising rates could prove to be negative for the crown, especially in the current global environment where economic activity is slowing," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch. "We'll see a negative impact on the economy from any rate hike and that is hardly a recipe to attract portfolio flows into the crown." \par \par \uc2  MacKinnon forecast the crown at 9.35 on a one-month horizon against the euro, just beyond a 2-1/2 year trough set on June 7. He saw the crown weakening beyond 11.00 against the dollar. This would take it close to record low of 11.0440 set on June 11. \par \par \uc2  The crown has been in a downtrend against the euro since May 2000, when it hit highs around 8.0430 - over 10 percent stronger than current levels. It has been on a downtrend against the dollar since 1996 when it hit highs around 6.4250 crown per dollar - more than 40 percent stronger than current levels. \par \par \uc2  Seven of 10 analysts surveyed by Reuters last week expected the Riksbank to leave rates steady on Friday, while three forecast a 25 basis point rate rise. \par \par \uc2  CHANGING TRENDS DIFFICULT \par \par \uc2  Traders said it would be difficult to change the trend in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had been hit by real outflows of funds from the country rather than just poor sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Change in Sweden's pension funds industry this year has been a key factor in the crown's weakness as funds are now allowed to invest in foreign assets. \par \par \uc2  Also, weakness in technolgy stocks this year has hurt the crown which tends to track Sweden's tech-laden stock market. \par \par \uc2  With Swedish economic data beginning to deteriorate in the current economic climate, a rate rise would only serve to harm the economy and hence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But with underlying inflation, the gauge upon which the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bases its monetary policy, hitting a seven-year high of 3.1 percent year on year in May, the Riksbank's options are looking limited and tough. \par \par \uc2  "The downward pressure on the Swedish crown is coming from portflio flows and not speculators," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  "The best the Riksbank could hope for is for the crown to consolidate in a range. To hike rates in a context of domestic economy weakening will not be welcomed so maybe it would be better not to move rates and just \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Riksbank is one of the only central banks that has not cut interest rates this year in the face of a global slowdown. It's key repo rate was last changed in December when it was raised by a quarter percentage point to 4.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  In contrast, the U.S. Federal Reserve has slashed 2.75 percentage points off the fed funds target rate so far this year. Even the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is faced with rising inflation, has cut euro zone interest rates by 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Chartists said the crown would need to strengthen almost four percent against the euro before the technical outlook turned brighter. \par \par \uc2  "The euro/crown's trend is up, up and up," said Steve Wesiak, technical strategist at ABN AMRO in Amsterdam. "The major part of the uptrend started in May 2000 and to break that you would need to take out 8.90." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7300fk2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
