\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Swedish finmin says crown  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  will work. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Patrick McLoughlin \par \uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 11:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, June 27 (Reuters) - Swedish Finance Minister Bosse Ringholm said on Wednesday he believed recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would succeed in supporting the Swedish crown. \par \par \uc2  "Absolutely," he told Reuters on the sidelines of a conference. "We have a quite independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Sweden. It's up to the Riksbank to decide, but of course I hope the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be successful in strengthening the Swedish crown." \par \par \uc2  The crown reversed early weakness against the euro and the dollar in the wake of his remarks, but remained weaker than when the Riksbank started buying earlier in the month. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have continued to test the Riksbank's resolve, driving Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further into territory last seen before the Riksbank started buying. \par \par \uc2  CROWN AND EURO "UNDERVALUED" \par \par \uc2  Asked if the euro was undervalued, Ringholm, who is also the current head of the European Union's Ecofin group of finance ministers, said: "Yes, I suppose both the euro and the Swedish crown will be stronger in the future because the economic situation in Europe and \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  is strong just now." \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Swedish crown against the dollar and the euro in recent sessions in a bid to repel inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  Its purchases temporarily stemmed a weakening trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but have failed to provide substantial support. \par \par \uc2  The crown pared early losses to last trade at 10.672 to the dollar against 10.685 late on Tuesday and 9.225 to the euro from around 9.238. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank has said the falling crown threatens its two percent inflation target, with Swedish headline inflation hitting a six-year high of 3.0 percent year-on-year in May. Underlying inflation, which is the main gauge monitored by the Riksbank, hit a seven-year high of 3.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  But Ringholm said he was not overly concerned by the latest data. \par \par \uc2  "In the last few months we have seen higher inflation in Sweden and Europe but at the same time there are special reasons for that so I don't think it is necessary to make final conclusions," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We will have to see in four, five or six months if it is more permanent inflation," he said. "In Sweden we have had very successful wage negotiations... so it is a good situation for calm inflation developments in the future." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6r00rzx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
