\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Swedish c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , crown climbs. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Starck \par \uc2 731 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2001\par 17:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, June 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the second trading day in a row by buying Swedish crowns, pushing the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  "We have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bought crowns," a Riksbank spokesman said. He declined to comment on volumes, against which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and at what level the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and analysts said the Riksbank had been in the market buying crowns against both the euro and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank had already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which it regards as distinctly undervalued - on Friday in what it said was a monetary policy action to combat the inflationary impact of an excessively weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The crown jumped by 0.8 percent against the euro and by 1.1 percent, against the dollar in the wake of Monday afternoon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, but later eased somewhat. \par \par \uc2  The crown, which hit on Monday its firmest levels against both the euro and the dollar since May 25, has now strengthened by 3.8 percent against the dollar and by 2.3 percent versus the euro compared with levels last Thursday afternoon before Governor Urban Backstrom warned in a speech that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be ruled out. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Riksbank had been buying crowns on Monday against the euro at around 9.07-9.10 crowns per euro and later at 10.60 and firmer levels against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  FOUR PERCENT OF RESERVES \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated that Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  totalled around 300 million euros, or roughly the same amount as on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Guillaume Salomon, an analyst at UBS Warburg, told Reuters it seemed that the Riksbank had spent around four percent of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in its repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday and Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Initially, what they want to do is to break the trend," Salomon said, referring to the Riksbank's stated purpose for the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have an exchange rate target for the freely floating crown. But it has said that the steady weakening until Friday of the exchange rate is posing a threat to its two percent inflation target. \par \par \uc2  Riksbank Governor Urban Backstrom said on Saturday he believed the crown's weakening by double-digit percentage figures against the euro and the dollar in the past year, a trend which has recently accelerated, was due largely to a market psychology, which he likened to the boom and bust in information technology shares in 1999-2000. \par \par \uc2  "This can feed on itself and that's why we wanted to enter the market with full strength and send a signal that this is wrong," he said in an interview on Swedish radio news. \par \par \uc2  SHOWING THE FLAG \par \par \uc2  "We wanted to show the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, hoist the flag, that something is odd with the Swedish crown." \par \par \uc2  Mans Grunberger, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at SEB Merchant Banking, told Reuters it was difficult to say whether the Riksbank would be back in the market again later this week. \par \par \uc2  "The Riksbank has shown that it is very determined to strengthen the crown so it (more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) cannot be excluded," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It is hard to say if there will be more support purchases because they are now back at the crown levels that prevailed at the time of the latest inflation report when the bank did not express any worries about the crown," said John Kyriakopoulus, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan. \par \par \uc2  At 1455 GMT the crown was quoted at 9.0525 against the euro and at 10.5085 per dollar compared with 9.1209 and 10.5951 respectively at midsession. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank stressed last week it did not have any exchange rate target for the crown but was intent on preventing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness from hindering its efforts to steer inflation back towards its two percent target. \par \par \uc2  Swedish headline inflation hit a six-year high of 3.0 percent year-on-year in May with underlying inflation, which is the main gauge monitored by the Riksbank, at a seven-year high of 3.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  "It is the crown's development which has caused the inflation risks to look somewhat different now," Backstrom said in the radio interview. (Additional reporting by Johan Sennero and Jenny Andersson in Stockholm). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6i01a24\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
