\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic stocks trade sideways, Statoil debut flat. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Patrick McLoughlin. \par \uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2001\par 18:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, June 18 (Reuters) - Norway's Statoil dribbled back to its IPO at the end of its first day of trade on Monday, setting the tone for flat Nordic markets, while Finland's Elcoteq dropped 14 percent on a profit warning. \par \par \uc2  Renewed profit worries, looming regional holidays and wariness ahead of results from U.S. software maker Oracle reduced trading in Nordic stocks to a near-torpor. \par \par \uc2  "The trade is pathetic because buyers are starting their summer holidays," one Helsinki broker said. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of nervousness around technology earnings and that will continue to weigh on the sector," a Copenhagen dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The region's benchmark Stoxx Nordic index was down 0.03 percent as two off the region's four bourses closed, outperforming the FTSE Eurotop 300 index by half a percent. \par \par \uc2  Finnish telecoms equipment heavyweight Nokia - which last week was rocked by major selloffs after a profit warning - was down half a percent, with investors weighing the implications of after a warning from Canadian rival Nortel Networks on Friday.. \par \par \uc2  "Nortel's profit-warning was bad news for Nokia, but not as bad as some first thought," a broker said. \par \par \uc2  "The mentality in general is that no positive news is anticipated, instead the market hopes for as few profit warnings this week as possible," another said. \par \par \uc2  Swedish competitor Ericsson shed 2.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  STATOIL SHEDS EARLY GAINS \par \par \uc2  Norwegian oil company Statoil opened at 72 crowns, above its IPO level, as the Nordic region's biggest listing since that of Swedish telecom operator Telia got under way. But profit takers pushed the stock back to its listing price. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the share issue - which had been four times oversubscribed - supported the view that a tentative recovery in the IPO market was gathering momentum. \par \par \uc2  "It's a huge amount of money and it's healthy that most of the issue, about 78 percent, was bought by investors outside Norway," said Danske Securities oil analyst Bjorn Jacobsen. \par \par \uc2  Nokia and Ericsson supplier Elcoteq dived into the red as much as 19 percent at its intraday low after the company warned weaker market conditions would force it to post a "clear loss" in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  Forestry stocks were mixed. Investors continued to weigh the impact of a profit warning by Finnish papermaker M-Real last week and the effect on dollar-earning companies of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday and Monday, which pushed up the value of the crown. \par \par \uc2  Brokers said the market had priced in 1 weak crown and the impact of a Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Swedish paper stocks - many of whom have big \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. and products priced in dollars - saw some investors offload positions. \par \par \uc2  Swedish groups Holmen and Assi Doman , which were off Friday, fell again by 0.7 percent and half a percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in combination with the profit warning (by M-Real), had some kind of trigger effect and there was some profit taking in those shares," said a Swedish head trader. \par \par \uc2  But fund managers said share prices in the sector had come off recently. "Valuations are reasonably cheap at the moment and buying on weakness is probably a good idea," said Gregor Smith at Aberdeen Asset Management. \par \par \uc2  (Additional reporting by Helsinki newsroom, Copenhagen newsroom, Oslo newsroom). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6i01a1x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
