\par\par \b \uc2  Riksbank unsure of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  success - governor. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Starck \par \uc2 887 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2001\par 15:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, June 16 (Reuters) - The governor of \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, said on Saturday it was premature to say whether Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which saw the crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverse a recent weakening trend, would achieve its purpose of staving off a growing inflation threat. \par \par \uc2  "As a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  you can never know if \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeed or not but we have a quite considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve and we are acting with full strength," Urban Backstrom said in a radio interview. \par \par \uc2  "It was good that it happened," he said, referring to the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance to two-week highs against both the dollar and the euro on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult to draw conclusions after the development over only one or two days, this is a longer perspective and we will have to see how it develops going forward." \par \par \uc2  Backstrom also told Swedish public radio the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been aimed at containing inflation and did not rule out raising key interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "I don't want to say anything concrete...we'll have to see when the time comes for us to do that. But we are below many other central banks which have cut rates and we are below the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (ECB) rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't want to bind myself on exactly how much it would be, in such a case (that the Riksbank were to raise rates)," he added. \par \par \uc2  He said the Riksbank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - approximately 160 billion crowns ($15 billion) - were substantial. \par \par \uc2  According to dealer estimates, Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in the region of three billion crowns. Dealers told Reuters on Friday the Riksbank had bought crowns for around 9.19-9.21 and later 9.1250-9.1450 per euro and also for about 10.58 per dollar . \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank confirmed on Friday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but declined to say by how much or at what levels which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been sold. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's key repo rate has been on hold at 4.00 percent since early December when it was raised by 25 basis points. The ECB's main refi rate was cut to 4.50 percent from 4.75 percent this spring. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank's executive board will hold its next monetary policy board meeting on July 5. \par \par \uc2  BOOM AND BUST \par \par \uc2  Backstrom said he believed that the crown's weakening by double-digit percentage figures against the euro and the dollar in the past year, a trend which has recently accelerated, was due largely to a market psychology, which he likened to the boom and bust in information technology shares in 1999-2000. \par \par \uc2  "It's a 'follow-the-leader' behaviour in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market where operators are acting not on the basis of the outlook for the Swedish economy but according to what they think others are doing," he said. \par \par \uc2  "This can feed on itself and that's why we wanted to enter the market with full strength and send a signal that this is wrong," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We wanted to show the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, hoist the flag, that something is odd with the Swedish crown." \par \par \uc2  Backstrom reiterated that the Riksbank, although convinced the crown is undervalued, did not target any particular exchange rate for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the purpose of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been to combat the inflationary pressure caused by the crown's depreciating external value. \par \par \uc2  "It is the crown's development which has caused the inflation risks to look somewhat different now," he said. \par \par \uc2  A soft \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  leads to higher prices of imported goods, in the current environment especially meat and petroleum products, the governor said. \par \par \uc2  WEAK CROWN HITS CONSUMERS \par \par \uc2  "It is completely clear that a falling crown exchange rate affects people's wallets," he said. "If the crown remains at a low level there is a risk of price effects elsewhere in our economy." \par \par \uc2  Unwavering action by the Riksbank was important from the point of view of maintaining the broad support and credibility enjoyed by the low-inflation policy. If the public's inflation expectations shifted upwards, "a price and wage spiral sets off again," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We will do our utmost to make sure that inflation remains at two percent," Backstrom said, stressing the longer-term nature of the Riksbank's monetary policy goal of on average two percent over a business cycle, which implies that monetary policy adjustments can be expected to take effect on a 12-24 month horizon. \par \par \uc2  Swedish headline inflation hit a six-year high of 3.0 percent year-on-year in May with underlying inflation, which is the main gauge monitored by the Riksbank, at a seven-year high of 3.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Now we have a situation where we lie above the inflation target. What is important is that we systematically aim at two percent when we conduct our policy," Backstrom said. \par \par \uc2  "Of course we could make sure that inflation would be next month exactly two percent by dramatically pulling the interest rate trigger. If we now quickly raise the rate to, say 15-20 percent, it could have rapid effects on inflation but this creates great instability for employment and production in the Swedish economy and people would soon lose confidence in the Riksbank's actions," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6g016pn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
