\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Swedish c.bank does not rule out  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Peter Starck \par \uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2001\par 16:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, June 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, said on Thursday it did not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the crown remained weak and posed an upside inflation risk. \par \par \uc2  "The Riksbank considers that in a fundamental perspective, today's weak exchange rate is not reasonable," Riksbank Governor Urban Backstrom said in the extract of a speech. \par \par \uc2  "If the crown remains weak for a longer period, there may be risk of inflation being higher one to two years from now." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Statistics Sweden (SCB) said consumer price inflation rose to a six-year high of 3.0 percent in May with underlying inflation, which forms the basis for the Riksbank's monetary policy, hitting a seven-year high of 3.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank's monetary policy target is two percent inflation on average over a business cycle. The target comes with a plus/minus one percentage point fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  Backstrom said the interest rate was the primary instrument for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with an inflation target. \par \par \uc2  "If there are grounds for believing that the crown will continue to be weak - and nothing else happens to alter inflation prospects - that will have consequences for monetary policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  But using the strongest and most direct language heard from the Riksbank since the crown began weakening against the euro a year ago and against the dollar in late 1999, Backstrom said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was another tool at a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's disposal. \par \par \uc2  "At a time when the exchange rate is a serious upside risk in the inflation forecast and deviates markedly from a reasonable value, a situation may arise where \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are motivated," Backstrom said. \par \par \uc2  The extract of his speech was titled "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot be ruled out". \par \par \uc2  The crown has weakened by more than 17.5 percent against the dollar this year and by more than one-third since mid-October 1999. Against the euro, the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen by 16 percent in the past 12 months and by 6.5 percent so far this year. \par \par \uc2  At 1345 GMT the crown was trading at 9.2089 per euro compared with 9.2358 at midday after the May inflation report but before Backstrom's speech. The crown also advanced slightly versus the dollar, to 10.8276 from 10.8298. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6e01l1u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
