\par\par \b \uc2  Swedish c.bank has no plan to support crown - paper. \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2001\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, Feb 21 (Reuters) - Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or Riksbank, has no plans to support the crown, which has weakened more than 10 percent in the past six months, Riksbank deputy governor Villy Bergstrom was quoted on Wednesday as saying. \par \par \uc2  "The issue is not even under discussion," Bergstrom told the financial daily Finanstidningen in an interview. \par \par \uc2  In autumn 1998, the Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the crown. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a member of the European Union but has not joined the third phase of Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) and the euro single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The crown is a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank's trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket TCW-index rose above 132 this month for the first time since July 1995. The higher the index, the weaker the crown. \par \par \uc2  At the time of the October 1998 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the TCW-index hovered just above 130. \par \par \uc2  Bergstrom told Finanstidningen a continued softening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  entailed a certain inflation threat down the road. \par \par \uc2  "But on the other hand experience tells us that a weaker crown no longer has the same impact on inflation as earlier," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank's inflation target is two percent on average over a business cycle. In December, Swedish inflation fell to 1.4 percent year-on-year from 1.7 percent in November. \par \par \uc2  Bergstrom said the Riksbank's next key rate move could be up or down. The bank's next monetary policy board meeting is scheduled for March 26. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank raised the repo rate to 4.00 percent from 3.75 percent in early December. \par \par \uc2  "At that time we believed in a series of rate increases this spring. But this sentiment has definitely turned," Bergstrom said. \par \par \uc2  "Now the March meeting will show where we are headed. If the supply side tightening continues an increase cannot be ruled out," he said. \par \par \uc2  "But it is clear that if there is a sharp (economic) downturn which hits our exports and if consumers begin to lose confidence, then it can be a (rate) cut," he added. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2l04zt0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
