\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Sweden \highlight\uc2 's Heikensten:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Reserves Right To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 1998\par 17:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reserving the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as long as this doesn't interfere with the inflation target, Sweden's Deputy Riksbank Governor Lars Heikensten said Wednesday, according to local newswire Direkt. \par \par \uc2  During a panel discussion at an economic seminar Heikensten stressed that the Riksbank intends to be careful with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however. \par \par \uc2  His comments comes after a surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Riksbank to support the krona last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Heikensten said this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was brought about by movements in the krona that were far beyond what most observers would consider reasonable, and added that the Riksbank believes that sharp volatility in the exchange rate isn't good for the economy. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1538GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duae0057m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
