\par\par \b \uc2  Swedish crown slide seen quashing easing prospects. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Abigail Levene \par \uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 15:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 14 (Reuter) - The flood of hot money out of the Swedish crown is set to continue, dampening chances of the rate cuts the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keen to make, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  The crown slid to its worst levels in a year on Friday, in a sharp extension of the downtrend which has seen it shed more than six percent of its value against the mark since October. \par \par \uc2  Traders blamed speculative sales, mostly by foreign players. \par \par \uc2  "It's nothing to do with fundamentals because you couldn't pick a country with better economic fundamentals," said Keld Holm, international economist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  The crown fell to a session low of 4.5790 per mark in afternoon Europe from Monday's close here around 4.5060/90. \par \par \uc2  Swedish Finance Minister Erik Asbrink said he was not worried by the soft crown. "With an inflation target and a floating crown this is something you have to be prepared for," he told journalists. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market had taken this as a green light to sell more crowns -- though they doubted that was what Asbrink had intended. \par \par \uc2  "The government wants rates to go lower and with the crown this weak the Riksbank won't cut rates," said Peter Lindquist, Nordic economist at HSBC Markets in Stockholm. \par \par \uc2  The market has been particularly chary of the Swedish unit since January, when Prime Minister Goran Persson pledged to spend 10 billion crowns on public services, Lindquist said. \par \par \uc2  Markets, fearing Sweden's two-year programme of fiscal toughness had been ended in a bid to woo voters, punished the crown on hearing of the plans. \par \par \uc2  Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, said this week that the crown was undervalued, but indicated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not yet reached a point where it had become a policy concern. \par \par \uc2  "The Swedish crown is easy to pick on -- the Riksbank doesn't have the same commitment as other central banks to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it's not in the ERM (exchange rate mechanism)," said Lehman's Holm. \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility rather than steer the crown, believing fundamentals will eventually drive it higher again, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The weak crown has put the Riksbank in an awkward position. In January, deputy governor Lars Heikensten said the soft \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had contributed to the bank's decision not to cut its key interest rate, the repo, since December 17. \par \par \uc2  Until then, the bank had been easing frequently with 25 cuts from early 1996 when the the rate stood at 8.91 percent. \par \par \uc2  In fact, expectations are likely to lean towards tightening as \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's position outside the EMS makes open market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasingly unsustainable, said Joe Prendergast, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  Yet that speculation, plus mild recovery prospects and high real rates, are unlikely to benefit the crown, he believed. \par \par \uc2  Insufficient fiscal progress and a lack of credible fiscal retrenchment plans for the near future are seen preventing Sweden participating in European monetary union, even in the event of stronger political will, said Prendergast. \par \par \uc2  -- London Newsroom +44-171-542-8968 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters L