\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : SEK Firmer Vs DEM On Lira's ERM Reentry \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 1996\par 13:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OSLO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Swedish krona is markedly stronger against the Deutsche mark around midday Monday in Europe. Stockholm dealers attribute the krona's strength to firming spurts for many European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the Italian lira's reentry to the European Union's exchange rate mechanism (ERM). \par \par \uc2  In spot trade at 1140 GMT, the Deutsche mark is fetching 4.3775 kronor, down from 4.3895 kronor in early Monday morning trade in Europe, and 4.4020 kronor late Friday. \par \par \uc2  'The krona's strength is all related to Italy re-joining the ERM,' said one trader with a major Stockholm bank. 'The move made a lot of investors unwind their long positions in the mark.' \par \par \uc2  However, Sweden's finance minister Erik Aasbrink said Sunday the entry of the Italian lira into the ERM won't affect Sweden's position regarding a possible entry of the krona. \par \par \uc2  'It is still the government's view that linking the krona to the ERM is not on the agenda,' he said. Aasbrink also said the decision by Italy to reenter the ERM will not increase the pressure on Sweden to do so in 'any significant way.' \par \par \uc2  Looking at the rest of the day's dealings, one Swedish trader said the krona's strengthening spurt could be slowed or halted if the Riksbank, \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. So far though, the Riksbank hasn't made an appearance, traders said early Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  It is part of the Riksbank's stated policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen volatility in the Swedish unit and it has done this on several occasions in recent months. \par \par \uc2  The same trader predicted the krona will move in a narrow range between 4.3750 kronor a mark and 4.3900 kronor a mark in the near term. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-11-96 \par \par \uc2  1200GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbp01dt7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
