\par\par \b \uc2  Nordic  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : SEK Softer Vs DEM; Moderate Trading Volumes \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1996\par 09:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  COPENHAGEN (AP-Dow Jones)--The Swedish krona is slightly softer against the Deutsche mark Wednesday morning in Europe in moderate volume dealings. But traders say in the light of the mark's broad strengthening pressure, the krona's holding up pretty well. \par \par \uc2  In spot trade at 0758 GMT, the Deutsche mark is changing hands at 4.3490 kronor, up from 4.3400 kronor late in the session in Europe Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'I think we'll see the krona topping at 4.3550 (kronor a mark) and bottoming at 4.3350 (kronor a mark),' said a head trader with a Malmoe bank. \par \par \uc2  A day earlier, the krona's rapid weakening triggered an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Riksbank, to dampen volatility, dealers said. The Riksbank bought kronor against the mark at around the 4.35-krona-a-mark level, according to dealers. However, in line with its normal policy, the Riksbank refused to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders also predict if the krona shows signs of making a sharp move Wednesday the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might well step in again to smooth things out. \par \par \uc2  However, the market has been taking the Riksbank's moves calmly so far since many traders say the Swedish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't appear to be targeting any particular level for the krona but favors instead low volatility. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-10-96 \par \par \uc2  0812GMT \par \par \uc2  1058 