\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS -  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  powers Swedish crown to highs. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Eva Ahlberg \par \uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, Oct 25 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  catapulted the Swedish crown to new heights today and analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now on a roll. \par \par \uc2  "There is definitely a change in sentiment taking place... The crown is like a Spike Lee film, it is doing the right thing," said Andrew Bosomworth, an economist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  The crown -- often seen as a peripheral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with the Spanish peseta and the Italian lira -- may now be on the way to 4.60 per mark. "Today's breakthrough means that the field is free for a move towards 4.60," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  A move to 4.50 in the longer term is also seen possible. \par \par \uc2  "The level of 4.50 is not utopian by any means. We are in a positive trend and 4.50 within a year is not at all unthinkable," said Ake Gustafsson, economist at Swedbank. \par \par \uc2  The crown broke through a year high in early trade as the Swedish Riksbank moved in to offer support. It touched a high of 4.7130 against the mark before falling back to stand at 4.7370/00 by 1430 GMT compared with 4.7840 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The crown was last trading as high as 4.60 on May 3, 1994. \par \par \uc2  Economists said that while basic economic problems remain for \b \highlight22\uc2 Sweden\b0 \highlight\uc2 , still considered a high-yielder, today's Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  served its purpose. \par \par \uc2  Sources said the Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to push the strengthening crown to new highs. "The more people see the Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the more optimistic they grow on the fundamentals," said Michael Dicks, an economist with J P Morgan. \par \par \uc2  Swedish inflation, the Riksbank's biggest enemy, has improved considerably in the past months, falling to 2.5 percent in September from 2.7 percent in August. \par \par \uc2  In April and May this year inflation was running above 3.0 percent, breaching the Riksbank target of 1-3 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Still, there are potential pressures," said Michael Dicks of J P Morgan. Among these are the fact that producer prices have risen more rapidly than consumer prices. \par \par \uc2  Economists also said the crown has been salvaged by Swedish export companies switching out of the weak dollar into crowns. \par \par \uc2  "What we are seeing now is being helped by export companies needing to cover short positions and by the Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These are technical factors which are good for the crown," said Bosomworth of Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts feel 4.50 is the level where the Riksbank may choose to enter the European Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM). "If it can be sustained at that level, then they may choose to join," said one economist. \par \par \uc2  Before then, the Social Democratic government will have to prove it can continue to cut the budget and keep inflation low even in a period of stagnating growth, economists said. \par \par \uc2  Riksbank Governor Urban Backstrom said earlier the time was not right for Sweden to join the ERM. "The crown is still undervalued and it is therefore the wrong time for Sweden to join the ERM," he told a banking conference. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103drap02qxf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
